      "text": "Root crops and tubers are concentrated carbohydrate storage organs. They were humanity's caloric insurance policy — underground, frost-protected, harvestable on demand, dramatically more calories per acre than grain in many conditions. The potato alone may have changed European history more than any political revolution."
